### 5. OPERATIONAL, FACTORING & REGULATORY DISCLAIMERS
5.1 **Bank Factoring & Credit Underwriting:** The Platform provides technical software infrastructure (invitation state machines, document viewer desks, and automated multi-way split payment calculations) to facilitate freight financing. The Developer is not a financial institution, credit broker, or lending entity. All freight underwriting decisions, interest rates, factoring agreements, and credit recovery risks remain exclusively between the participating financial institutions and the Client/Contractors.
5.2 **Goods-in-Transit (GIT) Insurance & Underwriting:** The Platform provides digital API integration and split settlement capabilities for accredited third-party insurance underwriters to issue policies and review claims documentation. The Developer is not an insurance underwriter or insurance broker. Policy terms, risk assessment, insurable interest validation, premium schedules, and actual claim payouts or repudiations remain exclusively between the participating insurance underwriters and the insured cargo owners/transporters.
5.3 **Transporter Verification & Roadworthiness:** The Platform enforces digital compliance requirements (upload of driver licenses, hackney permits, GIT insurance certificates, and truck video proofs). The Client remains solely responsible for the physical inspection, mechanical roadworthiness, cargo security, and transit safety of contracted vehicles.
5.4 **In-App Messaging & Disintermediation Shield:** The Platform incorporates automated algorithmic keyword and regex filtering to obfuscate personal contact details and prevent disintermediation between truckers and contractors. While the Developer engineers robust anti-circumvention filters, the Client is responsible for enforcing platform terms of service, merchant compliance, and executing sanctions or account suspensions against offending participants.
5.5 **Statutory Tax & Financial Accounting:** The Platform automates calculation of Value Added Tax (VAT at 7.5%) and Withholding Tax (WHT at 5%) on brokerage and consultant fees. The Client remains solely responsible for obtaining and maintaining corporate haulage permits and timely filing of tax returns with government authorities (FIRS/NRS, SCUML).

